// endpoint_edit_held_prompt.proto — EditHeldPrompt: EDITING a held prompt.
// DAEMON-HOLD TRAY section. Owner spec, 2026-09-23.
//
// The tray card's Edit button BEGINS an edit; the editor's composer COMMITS
// or CANCELS it. THE ARM IS THE STEP.
//
//   begin  — the daemon CLAIMS the held prompt as being edited. While the
//            claim stands, that prompt AND EVERY PROMPT QUEUED AFTER IT stay
//            held: none is delivered, not by a turn's end, not by a verdict,
//            not by a release. The claim is published two ways: the tray entry
//            carries HeldPrompt.editing, and the workspace's host view carries
//            HostWorkspace.held_prompt_edit, which is what puts the prompt's
//            content into the editor's input.
//   commit — the prompt's content is REPLACED with `said`. It keeps its place
//            in the queue, its old classification is discarded, and it is
//            reclassified through the ordinary classifier path; an interject
//            verdict then interjects exactly as any interject does. The claim
//            is retired.
//   cancel — the claim is retired with the content unchanged, and the queue
//            resumes.
//
// ONE CLAIM PER WORKSPACE. The claim is scoped to the workspace's HOST stream
// (WatchHostWorkspace): the editor that holds the input is the claimant, so
// the moment no host stream stands for the workspace the claim is retired as
// a cancel would retire it. A daemon restart retires it the same way — the
// claim is in-memory, and the host stream it was scoped to died with the
// process. No timer ever retires a claim.
//
// The prompt is identified by its TurnId — the TYPED ECHO TOKEN loop, exactly
// as UpdateHeldPrompt names one.

